.policy "ruff-async105-trio-sync-call" revision 2
.description "Await calls to trio's async functions such as trio.sleep; without await the call only creates a coroutine that never runs."
.language python
.mode steer
.scope include "**/*"

// Ruff ASYNC105 (flake8-async): a call of one of trio's async functions (`trio.sleep`, `trio.open_file`,
// `trio.lowlevel.checkpoint`, …) that is not the operand of `await`. It only builds a coroutine, which never
// runs. Inside an async def the fix (unsafe) adds the `await`.
//   async def f(): trio.sleep(1)           ← ASYNC105, fix: `await trio.sleep(1)`
//   async def f(): await trio.sleep(1)     not reported
#include "python/misc2-async.rr"

.violation ASYNC105(at: node, callee: symbol) code "ASYNC105" "Call to `{callee}` is not immediately awaited"
    suppress ruff "ASYNC105"
    fix add_await "Add `await`"
ASYNC105(c, q) :- async_call(c, _, q), async_trio_coro(q), !async_awaited(c).
add_await(c, _) :- async_ctx(c), field(c, "function", f) => insert_before(f, `await `).
